  "topography": {
    "project_purpose": "Vaultka is a yield optimization protocol on Arbitrum that offers automated vaults for leveraged yield farming, liquidity provision, and staking. Users deposit assets into various vaults (e.g., SakeVault, VodkaVault, Water) which execute strategies across GMX, AARK, and other DeFi protocols to generate returns. The protocol also features a governance token (VKA) with voting escrow mechanics and a suite of reward handlers and vesting contracts.",
    "relationship_narrative": "All contracts belong to a single Vaultka family, sharing a common governance token (VKA) and voting escrow system. Vaults like SakeVault and VodkaVault rely on handler contracts (e.g., VodkaV2GMXHandler) and reward handlers to interact with external protocols and distribute incentives, while proxy contracts provide upgradeability across the system.",
